# CoW true-lazy P3 tier-1 — POSITIVE witness: the borrow-flip FIRES.
#
# `String x = coll.get(0).unwrap()` is a read-only element bind: neither
# `x` nor the source collection `coll` is ever mutated in the function.
# The whole-function forward-scan proves it pristine, so the resource-bind
# borrow-flip turns the eager deep-clone into a zero-cost Ptr borrow alias
# (0 `gorget_string_clone_to_owned` calls vs 1 at baseline). Pure reads of
# `x` after the bind observe the element in place — same output as an
# eager clone, but without the allocation.
void main():
    Vector[String] coll = ["alphalonglonglongbuffer", "betalonglonglongbuffer"]
    String x = coll.get(0).unwrap()
    print(x)
    print(x.len())
